From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 86/86] PC5: a USB keyboard types in the console's language's layout,
 and the pointer hides only for a game that asks

A keyboard plugged into the PS5 typed as a US one whatever it was: on a
French AZERTY keyboard the key marked A typed q, and @ (AltGr+0) couldn't
be typed at all, for a game's login (World of Tanks). Its keys now reach
Wine by their place (input type 7, PW_WINE_INPUT_KEYBOARD_KEY), and Wine
patch 0992 sends them as the keys of the layout WINE_PS5_KEYBOARD names,
with its characters (tools/make_ps5_keyboards.py writes the 21 layouts
from xkeyboard-config). Unset or "us", nothing changes, and the keys a
controller's button mapping names keep their US places in every layout.

Wine patch 0999 no longer hides the pointer unless WINE_PS5_CURSOR_IDLE_MS
asks for it: PC5 sets it for a game whose Mouse pointer option says so.
